  every glob pytest collects answers True. It could not fail on a file
  the repo does not collect, so both surpluses above passed it. The
  converse is now driven against real pytest, in a throwaway repo
  configured by mcp-server's own [tool.pytest.ini_options] table.

  pytest --collect-only collects            ['tests/test_real.py']
  candidate                                  collected   is_test_file
  tests/test_real.py                         True        True
  tests/__init__.py                          False       False
  tests/conftest.py                          False       True
  tests/helpers_test.py                      False       False
  tests/fixtures/state_cycle_3.json          False       False
  src/tiny.py                                False       False
  src/helpers_test.py                        False       False
